  "notes": "General Music Studies Option (of two: General Music Studies, Music Technology -- General Music Studies chosen as the simpler/more general track; Music Technology needs INART/MATSE catalog data not yet built). New music_catalog.json created for the entire MUSIC department used by this plan. Real engine-mechanics gap (same pattern as Architecture B.Arch/AED/LARCH): MUSIC 122 and MUSIC 132 are mutual corequisites of each other -- broken into one-directional edges. 'Applied Music' (individual lessons) and 'Ensemble' are repeated every semester with no single canonical course code (they vary by the student's instrument/ensemble) -- modeled as generic slots throughout, same convention as WFED 395's specialization pool. 'BA Fields'/'BA World Cultures'/generic Gen Ed pools are modeled generically, same convention as CMPSC's own open pools. Entrance to Major (completion of a two-year core) and MUSIC 476W's 7th-semester-standing prereq are noted but not modeled as enforced gates, matching convention for standing-based requirements elsewhere in this session. 2026-08-27 re-verification against the real School of Music 2025-26 Undergraduate Handbook (sites.psu.edu/music/files/2025/09/UG-Music-Handbook-25-26-9-16.pdf) confirmed the rest of the plan row-by-row; the handbook has no further restrictive list for '400-Level Music' beyond 'any 400-level MUSIC course', unlike CMPSC's own narrower technical-elective categories -- a genuine open_elective candidate. Wired all 4 occurrences (12cr) to `open_elective` with `elective_min_level: 400`, restricted to the MUSIC department only (`elective_exclude_prefixes: [ENGL, ESL, CAS]`), and denylisted the independent-study/special-topics/internship/student-teaching codes (MUSIC 494/494H/495/495A/495B/495C/496/496H/497/499) plus MUSIC 476W (the B.A. Senior Project, already separately required in Semester 8) -- same convention as CMPSC's 400-level-elective exclusion of its own department's 494/495/496/499 codes.",
